# AGENTS.md — orientation for an AI assistant working on this book

You are looking at the finished output for **{TITLE}** by
{AUTHOR}, built for Amazon KDP. This file explains what is here, how it was made,
and how to change it when something is wrong.

Read this before editing anything. Several tools in this pipeline report success
while producing silently wrong output, and the workarounds are not obvious.

---

## 1. What this folder is

| Path | What it is | Uploaded to KDP? |
|---|---|---|
| `READ_ME_FIRST.TXT` | Plain-English guide for the author | no |
| `UPLOAD_THESE/1_PAPERBACK/` | Paperback interior + cover wrap | **yes** |
| `UPLOAD_THESE/2_HARDCOVER/` | Hardcover interior + cover wrap | **yes** |
| `UPLOAD_THESE/3_KINDLE_EBOOK/` | EPUB + ebook cover JPG | **yes** (EPUB only) |
| `UPLOAD_THESE/3_KINDLE_EBOOK/EXTRA_for-device-proofing/` | AZW3 / MOBI | **no** — sideload only |
| `CONTENT_TO_PASTE/` | Listing copy, one file per KDP form field | pasted, not uploaded |
| `PROOFS/` | Cover proofs with trim/safe/barcode guides | no |
| `EDITABLE_SOURCE/` | Formatted `.docx` and `.odt` | **no** — for editing only |
| `scripts/` | Everything needed to rebuild all of the above | no |

### Book facts you must not get wrong

```
Trim ............ {TRIM}
Pages ........... {PAGES}  (print PDF; the DOCX/ODT differ - see §6)
Paper ........... {PAPER}
Paperback spine . {PB_SPINE} in
Hardcover spine . {HC_SPINE} in
Hardcover panel . {HC_PANEL}  (boards overhang the text block)
Hardcover hinge . {HC_HINGE} in each side of the spine, must stay clear of text
```

**Page count drives spine width drives the cover.** If you change anything that
alters the page count, the covers are invalid until rebuilt. This is the single
most likely way to ruin this job.

