## 2. Where the scripts are and how to run them

Everything lives in `scripts/`, which is a self-contained clone of the working
directory. It has been tested from a cold start and reproduces this output
byte-for-byte in structure.

```
scripts/
├── book.json                     the config: metadata, palette, paths, listing copy
├── front cover.png               source art (8.5 x 11, 432 dpi)
├── back cover.png                source art
├── {MANUSCRIPT}   the original manuscript
└── build/
    ├── all.sh                    3-pass interior PDF build
    ├── build_everything.sh       full rebuild of every format
    ├── topdf.sh                  HTML -> headless Chrome -> PDF
    ├── extract.py  model.py      manuscript .docx -> structured book.json
    ├── typo.py                   curly quotes, em dashes, ellipses
    ├── render_html.py            book structure -> print HTML
    ├── paginate.py               forces chapter openers onto right-hand pages
    ├── finalize.py               folios, running heads, epigraphs, mirrored margins
    ├── cover.py                  front / back / spine / wrap / ebook cover / proofs
    ├── epub_build.py             EPUB 3
    ├── docx_build.py odt_build.py   editable formats
    ├── kdp_calculator.py         queries KDP for real cover geometry
    ├── package_kdp.py            builds UPLOAD_THESE/, PROOFS/, root README
    ├── write_listing.py          builds CONTENT_TO_PASTE/
    ├── verify.py                 post-build assertions
    ├── fonts.py                  re-download/instance the type family
    ├── fonts/static/*.ttf        Lora, Oswald, Source Sans 3 static instances
    └── *.json                    derived intermediates (see §5)
```

### Running it

```bash
cd scripts

# full rebuild, everything
PY=python3 ./build/build_everything.sh

# just the interior PDF (3 passes: pagination -> TOC page numbers -> final)
PY=python3 ./build/all.sh

# just the covers (both bindings)
python3 build/cover.py

# repackage the handover folders
python3 build/package_kdp.py --pages {PAGES}
python3 build/write_listing.py
```

`PY` overrides the interpreter; `CHROME` overrides the Chrome binary in
`topdf.sh`. Output lands in `scripts/dist/` — copy files up one level when you
are satisfied, do not let a half-finished rebuild overwrite the shipped folders.

### Dependencies

```bash
pip install python-docx pypdf pillow reportlab fonttools pypdfium2
brew install --cask calibre libreoffice        # ebook-convert, soffice
brew install pandoc imagemagick epubcheck
```

Google Chrome is required for the print PDF. There is no LaTeX in this pipeline.

