## 7. Traps that report success while producing wrong output

Every one of these cost real debugging time. If something looks inexplicable,
check here first.

- **Chromium print CSS:** `break-before: right` lands on even pages; `left` is a
  no-op. See §3.
- **A block whose height equals the page box, plus `page-break-after`, emits a
  phantom blank page.** Let natural height drive full-page elements.
- **Justified text needs `<html lang="en">`** or Chrome will not hyphenate.
- **A missing glyph becomes a Type3 font.** A `★` the display face lacks made
  Chrome synthesise one; it was replaced with a drawn rule.
- **reportlab declares an unused, non-embedded `/F1 Helvetica` on every page.**
  Pass `initialFontName=<a registered TTF>` or font audits fail on a file whose
  visible text is fully embedded.
- **LibreOffice's PDF export silently drops auto-inserted blank pages.** This made
  correct recto placement *look* broken. Always export with
  `'pdf:writer_pdf_Export:{"IsSkipEmptyPages":{"type":"boolean","value":"false"}}'`.
- **ODF `style:page-usage="right"` disables `<style:header-left>`**, leaking the
  chapter title onto versos. Fixed with two master pages chained by
  `style:next-style-name`.
- **python-docx:** `"Book Title"` is a builtin *character* style — adding it
  returns something with no `paragraph_format`. Custom styles are prefixed `OCS`.

